 `jira-reb-7141` tagged `imported:reconciler-bootstrap`.\n- So one local ticket produced two Jira issues: the first create was not recorded as the binding, a second create was, and the first issue came back inbound as a duplicate ticket.\n- The closed bug `21fc-51d7-90ca-4a03` covers the same symptom on Jira DC (index lag in recover_pending). REB is a Jira Cloud project, so that fix's scope does not establish the Cloud path is covered.\n\n## Not established\n- Which pass created REB-7141 and why its key was not recorded (lost response, timeout, recover_pending search miss on Cloud). The reconciler's run logs for 2026-11-12 14:00-15:40Z have not been read.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The pass that created REB-7141 and the reason its binding was not recorded are identified from reconciler logs or bridge state.\n- [ ] Either the Cloud create path is fixed with a regression test that drops the create response and asserts one issue results, or the cause is shown to be already fixed with the commit named.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["bridge"],"ticket_id":"7bed-62ad-fbc3-462f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Outbound create for sweating-revolting-oriole left an orphan Jira issue (REB-7141) that the reconciler re-imported as a duplicate ticket","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9262a774-cf6d-4ced-bf13-c4351c95eb2b","6d4d1d76-e0d0-46be-b6ee-afbb7fbc28d9"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795027432456822679,"uuid":"14a4f4bc-0fdf-45dc-ab9d-e164117dc09b"}